  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by hand and got the same result by running it.\n\n1. `service2` only imports two modules: `pricing.base_fee` and `discounts.apply_discount`.\n2. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**.\n3. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` applies gold's 20% discount: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**.\n\nNeither `decoy_tax.py` nor `decoy_shipping.py` is imported, so they have no effect. `decoy_tax.py` also has a \"gold\" entry (25%), but it isn't on the call path.\n\nANSWER: 480",
